# Testing discipline

## Required behavior

- Prefer deterministic tests; isolate network/time/randomness.
- Cover the layer you changed (Table vs HTTP) instead of only distant smoke.
- Do not delete or skip failing tests to “make CI green” without fixing the bug or an explicit waiver.
- Match the project’s PHPUnit (or existing) stack — do not impose Pest/Laravel Dusk by default.

## Anti-patterns

- Controllers-only coverage for Table rule changes
- Marking tests skipped to hide regressions
- Inventing a new test framework unasked
